work_experience:
  - company: HCL Technologies
    title: ML Infra Engineer (at Meta)
    location: New York, NY, USA
    start: 2024-03
    end: 2025-07
    current: false
    bullets:
      - Architected and deployed Sherlock, a production agentic AI system (fine-tuned LLaMA + RAG) to autonomously resolve ML infrastructure queries.
      - Engineered monitoring/doctor tooling in PyTorch for production LLM health with real-time alerting on entropy explosions, weight deviations, and throughput degradation.
      - Delivered end-to-end infra across the experimentation and model deployment lifecycle: CUDA kernels, distributed training, model optimization.
  - company: Tarifica
    title: Software/Data Engineer
    location: New York, NY, USA
    start: 2023-06
    end: 2024-02
    current: false
    bullets:
      - Built 300+ Python/BeautifulSoup web scrapers and Flask RESTful ETL pipelines feeding PostgreSQL analytics under strict latency requirements.
  - company: Amazon
    title: Software Development Engineer
    location: Seattle, WA, USA
    start: 2022-07
    end: 2023-03
    current: false
    bullets:
      - Designed and operated mission-critical AWS microservices (EC2, Lambda, CloudWatch) powering Amazon Go / Just Walk Out stores.
      - Led migration of a high-traffic service to AWS, cutting cost, latency, and support tickets via automated CI/CD.
      - Shipped production features across Java, Kotlin, Python, TypeScript, and Ruby on Linux.
  - company: Microsoft
    title: Data Science Student Research Fellow
    location: New York, NY, USA
    start: 2021-06
    end: 2021-07
    current: false
    bullets:
      - Extended the Financial Times police-complaints study in R, uncovering race/gender patterns across NYC, Chicago, Philadelphia datasets.
      - Built regression/ML models and presented findings to Microsoft Research scientists.

